00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:47,380
If I try to force them together, my brain just stutters.

293
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,060
The two rules are in total violent contradiction.

294
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:54,340
And when two rules fight like that, you have discovered a crack in your idea.

295
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:56,820
We often try to ignore these cracks.

296
00:13:57,020 --> 00:14:00,320
We try to rationalize them away because remapping is hard work.

297
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:00,760
It is.

298
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:04,220
But reality doesn't bend to accommodate a broken map.

299
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:12,080
If you hold a belief where two underlying constraints fundamentally contradict, the structure is objectively broken.

300
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:15,780
Fixing it doesn't mean you have to throw away everything you know.

301
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:22,500
It means you have to locate the exact, precise intersection where the constraints fail to overlap.

302
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:28,120
But the sources we're looking at take this concept of a crack and scale it up to an insane degree.

303
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:33,020
There's a paper in this collection called Obstruction Co-homology and the Topology of Failure.

